Create an automated chemistry assistant that takes balanced reaction equations, starting reactant masses, and a harvested product amount to determine the limiting reactant, theoretical yield, and percent yield based on principles from Chemistry 2e (OpenStax) — Chapter 4: Chemical Reactions and Stoichiometry. To avoid manually compiling atomic mass tables or writing custom string tokenizers, use the chempy library to parse molecular formulas into exact molecular weights and verify reaction stoichiometry against compound data from the NIH PubChem Database. The program outputs an organized breakdown of limiting reagent status, product yields, and remaining masses of unreacted species. Also use the heat of the reaction to determine if it is exothermic or endothermic, and compute the heat flow per mole of the product. 

Yes. This is actually a very strong final project idea because it naturally satisfies most of the Drafter requirements while also demonstrating real chemical-engineering knowledge.
Project Concept
Chemistry Reaction Assistant
A web application that allows users to:
Enter a balanced chemical reaction.
Enter initial reactant masses.
Enter an actual harvested product mass.
Calculate:
Molar masses (using Chempy)
Moles of reactants
Limiting reactant
Excess reactants
Theoretical yield
Actual yield
Percent yield
Remaining reactant masses
Heat of reaction (ΔH)
Exothermic vs Endothermic classification
Heat released/absorbed per mole of product
The application can also save calculations to a reaction history log.
